## 2. Employment Policies

### 2.1 Employment Status and Classification

All employees are classified based on their role and level, which determines eligibility for certain benefits and compensation structures. The primary levels are: **Individual Contributor (IC)**, **Manager**, **Director**, and **Vice President (VP)**.

### 2.2 Compensation and Payroll

MedSync Health is committed to competitive and equitable compensation. While individual pay is confidential, the following are the **FY 2024 Average Total Compensation** figures by level, reflecting our investment in talent:

| Employee Level | Average Annual Compensation (AED) |
| :--- | :--- |
| Individual Contributor (IC) | 294,000 |
| Manager | 441,000 |
| Director | 661,500 |
| VP | 1,102,500 |

### 2.3 Employee Referral Program

We encourage all employees to help us grow our team. The Employee Referral Program is governed by **HR-006 (Referral Program Policy)**. The following referral bonuses are currently in effect:

| Employee Level of Referred Hire | Referral Bonus (AED) | Eligibility Criteria |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| IC | 7,350 | Awarded upon successful completion of the referred employee's initial 90-day period. |
| Manager | 12,862.50 | Awarded upon successful completion of the referred employee's initial 180-day period, subject to departmental budget approval. |
| Director+ | 18,375 | Awarded upon successful completion of the referred employee's initial 12-month period, subject to executive review and a 50% payout deferral until the 18-month mark. |

***Note on Referral Bonuses:*** *The amounts listed above are subject to change without notice and are intentionally structured to reflect a combination of base pay, performance incentives, and a portion of the referred employee's potential first-year bonus, making the final payout amount **ambiguous** until all criteria are met.*

